1. EDUCATIONAL PURPOSE ONLY
   This software is a controlled academic simulation tool designed exclusively
   for cybersecurity awareness training, academic research, and demonstration
   of social engineering vulnerabilities. It is to be used only in supervised,
   sandboxed environments with explicit authorization from all relevant parties.

2. PROHIBITED USES
   The following uses are STRICTLY PROHIBITED:
   ❌ Deploying against any real user or system without their explicit written consent
   ❌ Using to harvest real credentials, passwords, or personal information
   ❌ Using outside of controlled, authorized, and sandboxed environments
   ❌ Distributing as part of any malicious phishing campaign or attack toolkit
   ❌ Using for social engineering attacks against any organization or individual
   ❌ Using in any manner that violates applicable laws or institutional policies

3. COMPLIANCE WITH LAWS
   Users must comply with all applicable local, state, national, and international
   laws. This includes but is not limited to:
   - India:  Information Technology Act 2000 (Sections 43, 66, 66C, 66D)
   - USA:    Computer Fraud and Abuse Act (CFAA)
   - UK:     Computer Misuse Act 1990
   - EU:     General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR)

4. LIABILITY
   THE AUTHOR(S) SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES, OR OTHER LIABILITY,
   WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM, OUT OF OR
   IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE SOFTWARE.
   The author bears no responsibility whatsoever for any misuse of this tool
   outside of its intended academic and educational scope.

5. INDEMNIFICATION
   You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the author(s) from and
   against any and all claims, liabilities, damages, losses, costs, expenses,
   or fees (including reasonable attorneys' fees) arising from your use of
   the Software or your violation of any of these terms and conditions.

┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                               PENALTIES FOR VIOLATION                                                │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Under Indian IT Act 2000:
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Section 66C  (Identity Theft)              → 3 years imprisonment + ₹5 lakh fine                                   │
│ Section 66D  (Cheating by impersonation)   → 3 years imprisonment + ₹1 lakh fine                                   │
│ Section 43   (Unauthorized access)         → Compensation up to ₹1 crore                                           │
│ Section 66   (Computer-related offenses)   → 3 years imprisonment or ₹5 lakh fine                                  │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Under US Federal Law (CFAA):
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Unauthorized computer access               → Up to 10 years federal prison + $250,000 fine                         │
│ Phishing / credential fraud                → Up to 20 years under wire fraud statutes (18 U.S.C. § 1343)           │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

Under UK Law (Computer Misuse Act 1990):
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Unauthorized access                        → Up to 5 years imprisonment                                             │
│ Unauthorized access with intent            → Up to 10 years imprisonment                                            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

